    "body": "Reopened. The maintainer still sees this defect in v0.25.0, which has the fix of PR #2446. He wrote in chat on 2026-11-22: \"bug; P1; no visible voxel body during simulation\". He sent a screenshot. It is not attached here.\n\nWhat the screenshot shows:\n- The build is v0.25.0, commit 7e2a8119, built 2026-11-22 02:53 UTC.\n- The Simulate tool is active. The playback bar reads `2D Offset1 · F 1200 mm/min · 15.9/1392.8 s`.\n- The viewport shows the tool, the Vise 125 mm fixture and the WCS axes. It shows no stock body and no voxel body.\n- The Browser tree shows the Stock row, the fig8 model and the operation 2D Offset1 with the hidden-eye icon.\n- The operation has 8318 moves and 5 warnings. The status bar says: \"Carried stock: the operation's top Z20.000 is below the material over its region (Z22.000) - the first de...\".\n- The machine is VMC 3-AXIS. The post is Siemens 840D. The setup is Setup1 with G54.\n\nNot known yet: if the stock is absent from the start of the playback or only after it starts, and if the hidden-eye icon of the Stock row is the cause or only a symptom. Check first if a hidden Stock row hides the simulation stock body, and if the carried-stock warning changes the drawn body.\n\nThe priority is raised from P2 to P1 on the word of the maintainer. A simulation without a visible stock body hides every gouge and every collision from the user.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
